# CreatorOps Studio environment variables (planned).
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. Real .env files are git-ignored.
# Placeholder values only. Never commit real secrets.
#
# DATABASE_URL: PostgreSQL connection string used by the API (Phase 1).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://creatorops:change-me@localhost:5432/creatorops
#
# AUTH_MODE: authentication mode for the API; "mock" until real auth exists (Phase 1).
# AUTH_MODE=mock
#
# API_BASE_URL: public base URL of the API, used by the dashboard and extension (Phase 1).
# API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# WEB_ORIGIN: origin of the web dashboard allowed by CORS (Phase 1).
# WEB_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
#
# EXTENSION_ORIGIN: origin of the Chrome extension allowed by CORS (Phase 1).
# EXTENSION_ORIGIN=chrome-extension://<the 32-letter extension id>
#
# SESSION_SECRET: secret used to sign sessions; must be replaced with a long random value (Phase 1).
# SESSION_SECRET=change-me
#
# HOST: interface the API listens on. Loopback by default; use 0.0.0.0 only deliberately (containers).
# HOST=127.0.0.1
#
# PORT: API port (default 3000).
# PORT=3000
#
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX: requests per minute per client address (default 300).
# RATE_LIMIT_MAX=300

# NODE_ENV: development (default), test or production.
# NODE_ENV=development
#
# DATA_DIR: where uploaded files are stored by the local filesystem adapter (default .data/media; a relative path is resolved against the repo root).
# DATA_DIR=.data/media
#
# TRUST_PROXY_HOPS: reverse proxies in front of the API whose X-Forwarded-For is trusted (default 0).
# TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=0
#
# ALLOW_MOCK_AUTH_ON_NETWORK: set true only on purpose; mock auth hands out tokens without credentials.
# ALLOW_MOCK_AUTH_ON_NETWORK=false
#
# LOG_LEVEL: fatal, error, warn, info (default), debug, trace or silent.
# LOG_LEVEL=info
#
# REDIS_URL: queue for background jobs (Phase 3). Optional for the API (jobs then wait in the
# database); required for the worker (pnpm dev:worker). Start a local Redis with pnpm dev:redis and
# print the URL with: bash scripts/redis-local.sh url. The password in the URL is redacted in logs.
# REDIS_URL=redis://default:change-me@127.0.0.1:6379

# SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY: 32 random bytes as base64. Encrypts provider API keys saved in the settings
# screen (D-066). Make one with: openssl rand -base64 32. Keep it out of git and different from
# SESSION_SECRET. Without it the settings screen cannot save a key. Losing it means re-entering keys.
# SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
# SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID names the key above inside stored values (letters and digits, default k1).
# SECRETS_ENCRYPTION_KEY_ID=k1
#
# FFMPEG_PATH / FFPROBE_PATH: the owner's own ffmpeg and ffprobe for the final video (D-086), a name
# on PATH (default) or a full path. Not bundled. Install: macOS
# `brew tap homebrew-ffmpeg/ffmpeg && brew install homebrew-ffmpeg/ffmpeg/ffmpeg` (plain `brew install
# ffmpeg` has no libass, so no subtitles); Windows
# `winget install Gyan.FFmpeg`; Ubuntu `sudo apt install ffmpeg fonts-thai-tlwg`.
# FFMPEG_PATH=ffmpeg
# FFPROBE_PATH=ffprobe
# SUBTITLE_FONT: font for the burned-in Thai subtitles (macOS Thonburi, Windows Leelawadee UI,
# Linux Loma or Noto Sans Thai). Missing Thai glyphs fall back to an installed font.
# SUBTITLE_FONT=Sans
